----------------------------------
INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS
----------------------------------

Optional files for Postfix MTA when using the MailScanner Milter

Copy the 'mailwatch-milter-relay' cron file into /etc/cron.hourly/

Link in /usr/local/bin the following files, so that they find functions.php in the MailWatch directory they come from
(adjust /opt/mailwatch to your installation path; a copy cannot find it):

# ln -s /opt/mailwatch/tools/Postfix_relay/mailwatch_postfix_relay.php /usr/local/bin/
# ln -s /opt/mailwatch/tools/Postfix_relay/mailwatch_milter_relay.php /usr/local/bin/

Verify if the 2 files are executable. If not, use "chmod +x" to correct this problem.

Note about mailwatch_postfix_relay.php and mailwatch_milter_relay.php:

The scripts have two options, run them with '--refresh' to process the whole log once,
or without arguments to process the log and then tail it continuously.

The 'mailwatch-milter-relay' cron uses the tail method: every hour it starts the scripts
again only if they are not running. Use '--refresh' only for a one-off reprocessing
of the log, e.g. after a logrotate, as it rereads the whole file.

ATTENTION:

Several files have changed their name and location in MailWatch 1.2.0, 
particularly the PHP files that are launched in cron and the Init script files.
Please read the documentation carefully to remove old files during the upgrade.